  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promotion of inter-community understanding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to increase constructive cooperation between communities and with local government. It is an effort to help them work constructively with each other to find solutions to community problems (of poverty, high unemployment, social isolation and social tensions).  Peace and Community Action (PCA) has developed an effective methodology of working intensively with small selected groups of community leaders and government officers to give them an understanding of non-violent approaches, and then supporting them as they apply their learning to their day-to-day lives, and build up self-confidence. 

The project ran in Matara District from 2007 to 2013, moving to Ampara District from 2013 to 2016 . It focuses on:  increasing trust, solidarity and community cohesion, and improved relations with government officers, so as to be able to tackle intra-community violence and find solutions to socio-economic problems; the establishment and strengthening of community-based organisations (CBOs) in every village; support for young people; and awareness programmes social problems; and inter-community exchanges to promote better understanding between different communities in Sri Lanka.  

Selected community leaders are helped to develop their own skills and strategies in order to resolve problems, facilitate long-term co-existence with others, and work together to achieve common goals; then encouraged to put their learning into practice by taking part in the implementation of community initiatives, and passing on what they have learned to neighbours and colleagues.</narrative>
  </description>
